25," A photo of a weasel on the back of a bird, which is now viral on Twitter, was taken by photographer Jason Ward and credited to Martin Le-May. The photograph was taken in a park in Essex, and the bird, a woodpecker, was carrying the weasel on its back, a struggle of life for both of them. Eventually, the weas Details: ,made the story public.
A photo of a weasel clinging to the back of a woodpecker, both in mid-air, has gone viral on Twitter, with over 7,0unic retweets. The photo was taken by photographer Jason Ward and credited to Martin Le-May, an amateur photographer from Essex, near London. The photograph was taken in a park in Essex, and the bird, a woodpecker, was carrying the weasel on its back, a struggle of life for both of them.
The story gained momentum as the British media soon picked up the story, and the television channel ITV interviewed Le-May. He explained that he was walking with his wife in the park and heard a distressed squawking noise, slightly in their direction, and soon realized that the bird had a small mammal on its back—a struggle for life for both the bird and the weasel. Eventually, the weasel lost its grip, and the bird flew away.",1006.3312638392672,37.2402223270147,4.7993549555540085,958.0159275378101,0.025563452010294856,1862,35615,0.2861220885693579,0.9622511399227618
