31," According to an interim report on the disappearance of flight MH370, the initial response to the incident was characterized by confusion and delays, with a five-hour gap between the last communication from the flight crew and the first distress signal, and an additional five hours before the first search flights took off. The report highlights delays and protocol violations before the launch of the search and rescue, and CNN's aviation correspondent Richard Quest identifies the delayed response as the most disturbing finding. The delay in launching a search and rescue for the missing plane continues to be a focus of attention for investigators and is likely to be a significant factor in any final report.",1006.3312638392672,37.2402223270147,4.7993549555540085,958.0159275378101,0.025563452010294856,1862,35615,0.2861220885693579,0.9622511399227618
