47," After being closed for over a decade, the Caminito del Rey, a cliffside hike in southern Spain, will reopen on March 26 following a $5.8 million reconstruction project. The trail, which features a boardwalk that hangs 100 meters above the Guadalhorte River, has been considered the world's most dangerous path due to its deteriorated state and fatal accidents in the past. The reopening coincides with Spain's Holy Week celebrations and will attract tourists to the area again, bringing new life to the surrounding village of El Chorro.",1006.3312638392672,37.2402223270147,4.7993549555540085,958.0159275378101,0.025563452010294856,1862,35615,0.2861220885693579,0.9622511399227618
