Answer: Tairod Nathan Webster Pugh, a US Air force veteran, was indicted on charges of attempting to provide material support to ISIS and obstruction of justice. The charges were based on evidence including a letter expressing allegiance to the terror group and a chart of crossing points into Syria. Pugh was denied entry to Syria by Turkish authorities.
